(4) The president of the Hart County Chamber of Commerce; and
(5) Three members who shall be appointed by the board of commissioners of Hart County.
(b) The members provided for in paragraphs (1) through (4) of subsection (a) of this section shall serve for terms of office as members of the authority which shall run concurrently with the terms of office which they otherwise hold as such officials. Designees shall serve at the pleasure of the official they represent. The three members appointed by the board of commissioners of Hart County pursuant to paragraph (5) of subsection (a) of this section shall serve for terms of office of four years, beginning on the first day of July, 1994, and on the first day of July every four years thereafter. Such members shall be eligible for reappointment. In the event of the death or resignation of either one of said appointed members, a successor shall be appointed by the board of commissioners of Hart County for the remainder of the unexpired term. No vacancy shall impair the power of the authority to act.
(c) The members of the authority shall receive no compensation for their services to the authority.

